  "reason": "The source assertion 'Astrocytes release complement proteins to tag and facilitate the removal (pruning) of new neuronal connections' describes an event where astrocytes cause a change in the state/availability of connections. The relation 'acts_on' is defined as 'SOURCE acts on or changes the state, position, or availability of the object TARGET'. This matches the causal action of releasing proteins to induce pruning (changing availability). Other relations like 'regulates' are too broad, 'caused_by' reverses direction, and structural relations like 'contain' do not fit the event-based nature of secretion causing removal."
